WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Clinical Research utilizes AI to enhance
perceptual, cognitive,

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.500
and decision-making intelligence across
three primary stages of the research

3
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:13.900
pipeline. Stage 1, investigational
development, uses AI to develop new

4
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.200
biological models, identify potential drug
candidates, and design treatment

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.560
pathways. Stage 2 involves trial conduct.

6
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.300
Here, algorithms optimize protocol
writing, patient selection,

7
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.700
and real-time monitoring to increase the
precision of the study.

8
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.800
Stage 3 covers data treatment. This
involves the settlement and communication

9
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.780
of personal and research data, where the
final results are synthesized.

10
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.960
These integrations drive medical
innovation, reduce clinical trial time,

11
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.660
and improve healthcare access. However,
this efficiency introduces critical

12
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.540
risks. Digitizing patient information
creates vulnerabilities in personal

13
00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:59.140
privacy, the authenticity of sources, and
the security of the research data

14
00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.360
itself. Furthermore, a lack of diversity
in training data leads to cultural

15
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.960
and racial biases. Applying a DEI
framework—diversity, equity,

16
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.460
and inclusion—is a technical necessity to
ensure the AI's conclusions are

17
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:20.220
valid for all populations. Stage 3
represents a critical point for governance.

18
00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.180
It is the moment where personal identity
is converted into raw,

19
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.980
manipulable research data.
